---
title: "Step 1 · Documents"
description: Upload, read and sort the documents of the period.
sidebar:
  order: 7
---

Step 1 holds every document of the period. It has two tabs: **Source Documents** and **Payroll**.

{% screenshot id="bookkeeping/documents-overview" caption="Source Documents: the document cards, the status filter and the folder view." /%}

## Upload documents

Select **Import documents** at the top right and choose the files. A whole folder can be dropped in at once. The documents need not be sorted first: Operon recognises the type of each file (bank statement, sales invoice, purchase invoice, payroll, other record).

Upload what the client sends later in the same way, at any time during the period.

## Reading: free and paid

After upload, the import window goes on to its **Read** step. Operon first checks each document: it sorts the documents by type and reads, at no cost, every document with a text layer and a known layout.

- **Read at no cost:** documents with a text layer (PDF, Excel, CSV, Word) whose layout is known.
- **Read by the model, after approval:** scanned PDFs and photos, PDFs without a usable text layer, and one sample of each layout not seen before (after the layout is learned, every document of that layout is read at no cost). When checking is finished, these documents are listed with the estimated cost. Select **Start reading (up to $…)** to approve the amount once for the whole import. A single document can also be read on its own with **Read with model (about $…)**. A document that is not approved is not read and is not booked; it is listed in the to-do list, where it can be approved with **Approve reading**.

A file that cannot be read is listed as a to-do item.

{% screenshot id="bookkeeping/documents-read-approval" caption="The Read step of the import window: all 12 documents read at no cost." /%}

## The document cards

The cards at the top group the documents of the period: **To classify**, **Sales invoices**, **Purchase invoices**, **Bank statements**, **Records and reconciliation**, **Marked as not needed** and **Outside this period**. On the bank statement card, a dot for each month shows whether a statement for that month has been uploaded.

## The status filter

| Filter | Shows |
|---|---|
| **To do** | Documents with an open question. |
| **Waiting for client** | Documents with a question on the client query list. |
| **On hold** | Documents set aside with a reason. |
| **All documents** | Every document of the period. |
| **Undetermined** | Documents whose type or treatment is not yet decided. |

{% aside type="caution" %}
Undetermined documents stop the quarter from being completed. Decide each one, or mark it as not needed, before step 3.
{% /aside %}

## Duplicates and statement accounts

When the same document is uploaded twice, Operon raises it as a duplicate; confirm or reject the match in the to-do item. When a bank statement could belong to more than one registered account, Operon asks which account it belongs to.

## Payroll

The **Payroll** tab imports payroll sheets or payslips. The payroll entries (salaries and CPF) are booked from them; see [Step 2 · Journal](/en/bookkeeping/journal/).
